{"name":"Floss","hex":"#d7b3b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floss","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thread used to clean the gaps between the teeth.","Raw silk fibres."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clean the area between (the teeth) using floss.","To show off, especially by exhibiting one's wealth or talent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dental floss","blocks":[{"text":"Dental floss is a cord of thin filaments, typically made of nylon or silk, used in interdental cleaning to remove food and dental plaque from between teeth or places a toothbrush has difficulty reaching or is unable to reach. Its regular use as part of oral cleaning is intended to maintain oral health."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/Floss4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dental_floss"},{"title":"Meat floss","blocks":[{"text":"Meat floss, also known as yuk sung or rousong, is a dried meat product of Chinese origin, with a light and fluffy texture similar to coarse cotton. It is more commonly known as bak hu in Hokkien-influenced regions, such as Southeast Asia and Taiwan. Meat floss is golden in color with a distinctive flavor and sweet taste that is somewhat comparable to beef jerky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Fragrance_Pork_Floss.jpg/330px-Fragrance_Pork_Floss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meat_floss"},{"title":"Floss (dance)","blocks":[{"text":"The floss is a dance and an Internet meme in which a person repeatedly swings their arms, with clenched fists, from the back of their body to the front, on alternating sides."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Floss_%28dance%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floss_(dance)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dental_floss_%28whole%29.jpg/500px-Dental_floss_%28whole%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dental_floss_%28whole%29.jpg/500px-Dental_floss_%28whole%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dental floss (waxed)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADental_floss_(whole).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Flossholders.jpg/500px-Flossholders.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Flossholders.jpg/500px-Flossholders.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"left: floss molded in disposable prongs,  top: 135° handle,  bottom: 90° handle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlossholders.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Embrasure_spaces.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Embrasure_spaces.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The classification of the amount of gum that fills the spaces between the teeth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmbrasure_spaces.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Powered_flosser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Powered_flosser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Powered flosser","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APowered_flosser.jpg"},{"srcs